// simple_sdf — flutter/samples/simple_sdf
//
// Not "no analogue" — the counterpart is strong — but not finished either.

fn screen_simple_sdf() {
    return counterpart_screen("Simple SDF",
        "Drawing signed distance functions with the FragmentShader API \u2014 sdHeart, folded on x, pink against black, smoothstepped over the zero crossing.",
        "makepad draws every one of its widgets with MPSL and ships a first-class Sdf2d API, so signed distance fields are not an exotic addition here — they are how the toolkit works. FlutterSdf is the sample's own GLSL transcribed into MPSL and compiled into splash-widgets, and `{t:\"sdf\"}` is a real node kind the translator emits.",
        ["The widget compiles, the node is emitted, and nothing draws. No shader error is logged.",
         "Two hypotheses were tested and both were wrong: that the emitted draw_bg override was clobbering the pixel shader, and that GLSL's single-argument vector constructors were failing to compile. Removing both changed nothing.",
         "The remaining suspect is the isolate VM a mounted Splash allocates — a widget this crate adds to the prelude may not resolve there, which is the same seam as the repo's one upstream PR. Unconfirmed.",
         "On the ArkUI backend there is no fragment-shader path at all, so this screen can only ever be a makepad one."])
}
